Install ironic driver deps via extras.

Ironic change I4de9cf96fd66ef3ddf3f55bb9e1850859a3fd82b removed
driver-requirements.txt, moving the two driver dependencies it
listed (ansible and networking-generic-switch) into pip extras of
the same names. The ironic-conductor image still installed
'-r /ironic/driver-requirements.txt', so image builds against
Ironic master now fail with:

    ERROR: Could not open requirements file: [Errno 2] No such
    file or directory: '/ironic/driver-requirements.txt'

Install the equivalent extras from the Ironic source tree at
/ironic instead. This keeps the list of driver dependencies
maintained in Ironic rather than duplicating it in Kolla.

Prompt: Debug why CI failed on kerbside-patches PR 1461, then
write a patch fixing the ironic-conductor image build so it can
be validated in private CI before being proposed upstream to
Kolla.

